WEBVTT

00:28.610 --> 00:31.370
It's remarkable how well they faired
against so many elves.

00:31.370 --> 00:34.760
Sure, but this location
has no strategic value whatsoever.

00:34.760 --> 00:35.770
I agree.

00:35.770 --> 00:38.810
- What they did is hardly worthy of praise.
- However, the fact they've diminished

00:38.810 --> 00:40.600
the Empire's forces does
help us in the long run.

00:40.600 --> 00:42.070
How do we punish them?!

00:42.070 --> 00:43.310
Don't you mean praise them?

00:43.310 --> 00:44.890
They defied Her Majesty!

00:44.890 --> 00:46.570
But they also helped save the Kingdom!

00:46.570 --> 00:49.200
And you think that makes them heroes?
Because I don't!

00:49.200 --> 00:51.110
Then, are you saying they're traitors?!

00:54.120 --> 00:57.390
Whether they wish to be
friend or foe to our Kingdom

00:57.390 --> 01:00.120
is something they can decide
for themselves.

01:01.900 --> 01:02.630
Theodore.

01:02.630 --> 01:03.750
Y-Yes, Your Majesty!

01:03.750 --> 01:05.230
Why are you so high-strung?

01:05.230 --> 01:07.260
I'm sorry, it's nothing.

01:07.260 --> 01:11.550
I just wasn't expecting you to personally
call me by name, Your Majesty.

01:11.550 --> 01:16.190
You're one of my most proud
and loyal servants, isn't that right?

01:16.190 --> 01:18.620
Yes! Without a doubt, Your Majesty!

01:18.620 --> 01:19.930
Good.

01:19.930 --> 01:23.840
Then I can trust you
to do something for me.

02:58.030 --> 02:59.810
What do you wanna eat, Nana?

02:59.810 --> 03:00.880
Beef or fish?

03:00.880 --> 03:02.960
Or is that some kinda cannibalism?

03:02.960 --> 03:04.840
But wait, sharks eat fish all the time.

03:04.840 --> 03:07.400
Anything okay.
Me hungry.

03:07.870 --> 03:08.500
All right.

03:08.500 --> 03:11.840
They'll be treating us to drinks
before any food, obviously!

03:11.840 --> 03:14.560
That's the standard way
to celebrate a victory, after all.

03:14.560 --> 03:16.070
Don't get your hopes too high.

03:16.070 --> 03:18.260
We broke out of their prison, remember?

03:18.260 --> 03:21.210
Yeah, but we destroyed
the Thinker's fortress to make up for it.

03:21.210 --> 03:23.980
That's right.
And we restored peace to their land.

03:23.980 --> 03:27.730
Well, I just hope that's enough
to convince them.

03:27.730 --> 03:31.370
I think I've already made it
crystal clear how valuable I am.

03:32.230 --> 03:34.400
Yeah, if you consider playing
with mud valuable!

03:35.400 --> 03:38.150
W-Well, clearly, the demand
for gunplay is much higher!

03:41.530 --> 03:45.030
Hi! Your heroes have returned!

03:45.030 --> 03:48.620
Thanks for waiting to get
the big party started...

03:55.880 --> 03:58.010
What's with the lousy mood in here?

03:58.010 --> 03:59.010
Where's our feast?

03:59.010 --> 04:00.450
So you came back alive.

04:00.450 --> 04:02.750
No kidding!
That shit wasn't easy, trust me!

04:02.750 --> 04:06.560
You orchestrate a prison break,
throw us all into pointless confusion,

04:06.560 --> 04:09.290
and charge into enemy territory
without permission.

04:09.290 --> 04:11.350
How dare you show your faces here!

04:11.350 --> 04:15.150
Does the concept of shame
just not exist in your world?

04:15.690 --> 04:17.820
We were told to come here.

04:17.820 --> 04:19.570
Who even are you, anyway?

04:19.570 --> 04:22.330
Hey, what the hell is going on here?

04:22.760 --> 04:24.080
- Silence.
- This is—

04:24.080 --> 04:25.800
You don't get to speak.

04:28.080 --> 04:31.190
We went and made winning
the war easier for you.

04:31.190 --> 04:32.210
Haven't you heard?

04:32.210 --> 04:35.190
- We destroyed the Thinker's fortress and—
- "The Thinker," you say?

04:35.190 --> 04:37.150
Is that one of the generals
from the Empire?

04:37.150 --> 04:37.840
That's right.

04:37.840 --> 04:39.460
He was a thorn in your side.
And we—

04:39.460 --> 04:43.300
But this "Thinker" person
was originally from your world.

04:43.300 --> 04:46.310
So all you've done
is clean up your own mess.

04:46.310 --> 04:47.570
Isn't that right?

04:47.570 --> 04:48.590
Well...

04:48.590 --> 04:53.280
We also freed all the elves.
Isn't that worth something?

04:53.280 --> 04:55.930
True. That is a significant feat.

04:55.930 --> 04:59.950
But again, it was a human from your world
who brainwashed them in the first place.

04:59.950 --> 05:01.420
That's not our fault. It was—

05:01.420 --> 05:03.070
Don't forget what happened before that!

05:03.490 --> 05:06.800
You wreaked havoc at the great prison,
freed all the prisoners,

05:06.800 --> 05:09.600
and let the enemy seize a fort
that was under your care!

05:09.600 --> 05:12.570
Furthermore, you've shown no efforts
to change your violent behavior,

05:12.570 --> 05:15.320
your ridiculous outfits,
or your disrespectful attitudes!

05:15.320 --> 05:18.420
And while I'm at it, what even are you?!

05:18.420 --> 05:21.600
I've never seen a demihuman
like you before.

05:21.600 --> 05:26.010
Do you realize how much commotion
you cause among our people

05:26.010 --> 05:28.390
by just walking around outside?

05:29.600 --> 05:30.600
Nanaue!

05:33.560 --> 05:36.730
So quick to resort to violence!
Nothing but a dumb fish, aren't you?

05:36.730 --> 05:38.800
Okay.
I see how it is.

05:38.800 --> 05:39.570
Excuse me?

05:40.050 --> 05:43.010
You were never going
to accept us, were you?

05:43.010 --> 05:47.120
You're like those freakin' loser cops
who catch perps just to bully them in the joint.

05:47.120 --> 05:48.580
You wench!

05:51.080 --> 05:54.350
That's what I mean! That attitude of yours
is downright disrespectful!

05:54.350 --> 05:58.340
Especially with all that silly makeup!
Know your damn place!

06:12.060 --> 06:12.980
Stop it!

06:18.590 --> 06:19.940
- C-Come, my sword!
- Not so fast.

06:21.320 --> 06:22.110
Shit!

06:22.610 --> 06:24.720
Are you trying to rip open
his stomach again?

06:24.720 --> 06:27.120
Like you did back at the prison?

06:28.150 --> 06:29.700
Answer me!

06:29.700 --> 06:32.390
Is this how you guys
do things around here?

06:34.910 --> 06:35.880
Huh?

06:35.880 --> 06:38.320
What are you standing around for?!
Attack, guards!

06:43.130 --> 06:44.680
Well, damn.

06:52.440 --> 06:53.790
What a pity.

06:53.790 --> 06:56.690
You should have known better than
to harm a subject of my Kingdom.

06:56.690 --> 06:57.900
"A pity"?

07:00.900 --> 07:03.090
That's rich coming from you.

07:03.090 --> 07:04.800
You're the one who made him do it.

07:04.800 --> 07:06.760
I have no idea what you're talking about.

07:06.760 --> 07:08.410
Execute them all immediately.

07:08.410 --> 07:09.870
Your Majesty, that's going too far!

07:10.290 --> 07:11.370
Cecil.

07:11.830 --> 07:13.370
Your Majesty!

07:17.960 --> 07:19.150
Fine, then.

07:19.150 --> 07:22.070
We'll only execute the demihuman.

07:22.070 --> 07:27.130
For your achievement in defeating two enemy
generals, the rest of you shall be exiled.

07:32.140 --> 07:33.970
H-Hey! Screw that!

07:34.400 --> 07:35.520
Back off.

07:52.730 --> 07:54.310
Please wait!

08:01.570 --> 08:02.460
What?

08:03.150 --> 08:04.690
Umm...

08:04.690 --> 08:07.210
This wasn't supposed to happen.
I'm really sorry—

08:07.210 --> 08:09.010
Can you quit with the apologies?

08:09.610 --> 08:12.170
"I'm sorry! Please forgive me!"

08:13.400 --> 08:16.480
Hearing that crap from you
just pisses me off even more.

08:16.480 --> 08:19.030
I thought there'd be a big feast.

08:19.030 --> 08:20.980
So did Nana.

08:24.480 --> 08:27.480
Jeez, you didn't even try
to stop her, did you?

08:27.480 --> 08:29.930
And after you guys
practically begged us for help.

08:29.930 --> 08:31.150
Well, uh...

08:31.150 --> 08:35.050
God, I hate you.
All you know how to do is talk.

08:35.050 --> 08:36.310
What was it you said before?

08:36.310 --> 08:39.770
Something about how it feels wrong
to just do what you're told?

08:39.770 --> 08:41.520
Don't make me laugh.

08:41.520 --> 08:43.240
If you're so afraid of disobeying mommy,

08:43.240 --> 08:45.560
then why don't you
be her little puppet forever?

08:46.830 --> 08:49.010
That's honestly preferable.

08:51.260 --> 08:53.830
Because then we wouldn't
have bothered to fight.

09:10.200 --> 09:13.240
Wow, sharp aim even when he's drunk!

09:13.240 --> 09:14.290
Yippee!

09:14.290 --> 09:16.480
- We won the bet! Drinks are on the house!
- He actually did it...

09:16.480 --> 09:17.770
Right, barkeep?

09:17.770 --> 09:18.830
Dammit.

09:19.560 --> 09:22.070
Fine, whatever.
Have at 'em, ya bastards.

09:22.070 --> 09:23.130
Thanks!

09:23.590 --> 09:25.130
Just this once, okay?

09:25.130 --> 09:28.720
I typically only show this trick
on very special occasions.

09:28.720 --> 09:29.860
Eh?

09:29.860 --> 09:32.380
Trust me, this will "melt" your hearts...

09:32.380 --> 09:34.010
Dundun Dun Dundun.

09:34.520 --> 09:38.180
Dundun Dun Dundun.

09:39.000 --> 09:42.770
Dundun Dun Dundun.

09:42.770 --> 09:45.090
Whoa, crazy! That's some weird magic.

09:45.090 --> 09:46.560
Wow. Totally bizarre!

09:46.560 --> 09:48.770
What?! You're supposed to be impressed!

09:48.770 --> 09:51.530
I just reenacted the most famous
movie scenes in cinema history!

09:51.530 --> 09:53.490
Huh? What's a "movie"?

09:53.490 --> 09:56.990
Oh, right. I forgot
that we're in an Isekai.

09:56.990 --> 10:00.540
What pitiful lives you must lead
without movies to entertain you.

10:00.540 --> 10:01.790
Listen, movies are...

10:02.330 --> 10:04.810
That's more than enough booze for you.

10:04.810 --> 10:06.670
Don't lump me in with the others!

10:07.250 --> 10:08.910
I never get drunk.

10:08.910 --> 10:11.610
Only assclowns lose all restraint
and drink themselves stupid.

10:11.610 --> 10:12.680
The key is tranquility.

10:13.190 --> 10:14.990
Keep your mind quiet

10:14.990 --> 10:19.470
and it'll open your eyes to the peace
at the bottom of the bottle.

10:23.480 --> 10:24.850
I don't feel so hot...

10:27.310 --> 10:28.750
There we go.

10:29.630 --> 10:31.250
You're still drinking?

10:31.800 --> 10:34.650
No better time to drink than right now.

10:35.880 --> 10:37.050
What's that?

10:37.050 --> 10:38.620
Oh, this? Pretty cool, huh?

10:39.110 --> 10:41.330
Just something I took
to make a retirement fund.

10:41.330 --> 10:43.000
So you stole it.

10:44.150 --> 10:48.130
C'mon. You better call it quits soon.

10:48.130 --> 10:50.670
Unless you wanna drink yourself to death.

10:50.670 --> 10:53.130
Wouldn't that be more convenient for you?

10:53.130 --> 10:54.000
What?

10:54.000 --> 10:58.490
I mean that old hag, your boss,
she's trying to...

10:58.490 --> 11:02.110
to take this world's... um...
whatcha call it...

11:02.110 --> 11:03.020
Resources?

11:03.020 --> 11:04.390
Yeah, that.

11:04.390 --> 11:07.810
She wants to take resources
from this world, right?

11:07.810 --> 11:10.640
And that's why she wants to end the war.

11:10.640 --> 11:15.990
But we failed.
We screwed the whole thing up.

11:15.990 --> 11:18.470
So we're useless now, right?

11:18.470 --> 11:21.950
Why not just blow us up? Like kaboom.

11:21.950 --> 11:23.640
What are you talking about?

11:23.640 --> 11:26.790
Without the radio signal from
the real world, your bombs are just—

11:26.790 --> 11:27.770
Say...

11:28.640 --> 11:30.190
Do you have a lover?

11:30.190 --> 11:31.190
Huh?

11:31.190 --> 11:33.920
Because I do. My Puddin'.

11:33.920 --> 11:37.770
And he's the best man in the world,
a real prince charming.

11:38.270 --> 11:39.840
You mean the Joker?

11:39.840 --> 11:41.760
I remember one time...

11:41.760 --> 11:47.370
Puddin' said everybody wants to find
a new world that's different from this one.

11:48.070 --> 11:49.600
And how they're all screaming,

11:49.600 --> 11:53.850
"This isn't who I really am!"
on the inside.

11:53.850 --> 11:56.400
Puddin' is a freakin' genius.

11:56.400 --> 12:00.600
Because that's how I'm feeling right now.

12:01.840 --> 12:04.330
Oh! Are you a minstrel?

12:04.330 --> 12:06.800
Tonight is especially vibrant with life!

12:06.800 --> 12:08.580
Please allow me to join you.

12:08.580 --> 12:10.210
How wonderful!

12:10.210 --> 12:13.050
There was a period of time
when I longed to live like that.

12:13.050 --> 12:14.470
Traveling from place to place

12:14.470 --> 12:17.990
and connecting all sorts of people
through song like a preacher!

12:17.990 --> 12:20.830
I am most humbled by your kind words.

12:20.830 --> 12:23.130
May I sing you a song?

12:23.130 --> 12:23.910
Of course!

12:23.910 --> 12:25.450
Let's hear it!

12:26.100 --> 12:28.450
Go ahead! The stage is all yours!

12:31.640 --> 12:38.590
♪ In the open sky above the battlefield ♪

12:38.590 --> 12:43.050
♪ There appeared a large box of metal ♪

12:44.910 --> 12:50.830
♪ Inside of it were warriors
itching for a fight ♪

12:50.830 --> 12:57.320
♪ Heroes from another realm ♪

12:58.260 --> 13:00.950
- Hey, these lyrics... What the?
- ♪ Wearing exotic outfits ♪

13:00.950 --> 13:03.260
- Will you stop singing that?
- ♪ And equipped with... ♪

13:04.140 --> 13:05.950
Hello, beautiful lady.

13:05.950 --> 13:07.320
You're welcome to leave your—

13:07.320 --> 13:09.100
I said, quit singing.

13:09.100 --> 13:12.030
They aren't damn heroes.

13:12.030 --> 13:15.760
Just a bunch of drunks who were abandoned
and exiled by the Kingdom.

13:15.760 --> 13:17.230
They're criminals!

13:18.470 --> 13:21.810
U-Uh, pardon me, miss!
The people in this song are actually—

13:21.810 --> 13:23.640
Are you deaf or what?

13:23.640 --> 13:26.240
She told ya to stop singing.

13:26.240 --> 13:27.070
Why?

13:27.070 --> 13:27.750
Huh?

13:27.750 --> 13:31.520
Why weren't any of my personal feats
mentioned in the song?!

13:31.520 --> 13:33.310
Is there more? A second verse?

13:33.310 --> 13:34.950
Please sing it!

13:34.950 --> 13:37.300
W-Well, then...

13:38.720 --> 13:41.590
When we say stop, you stop!

13:41.590 --> 13:42.800
Dammit...

13:42.800 --> 13:44.000
Huh?

13:44.000 --> 13:46.010
Don't interrupt him!

13:46.010 --> 13:48.350
Take it outside, you guys!

13:48.350 --> 13:51.910
Nice try, jackass!
You're never gonna hit me!

13:51.910 --> 13:55.800
Not while you're a third-rate hack who can't
get a leading role, much less be a hero!

13:55.800 --> 13:57.080
Nicely done.

13:57.080 --> 13:59.280
You really know how to piss people off.

13:59.280 --> 14:01.240
It's no wonder that
your family ditched you.

14:01.240 --> 14:03.870
Son of a bitch.
Now you've done it.

14:04.740 --> 14:06.730
This means war!

14:09.160 --> 14:11.200
All the time you spend playing with guns

14:11.200 --> 14:14.420
must have been so revolting to your wife
that it made her leave you!

14:14.420 --> 14:16.880
- Bastard!
- Aw jeez, don't come this way!

14:18.170 --> 14:21.880
Stop it... Please stop...

14:22.470 --> 14:25.750
P-Please help!
Do something to stop them!

14:25.750 --> 14:27.640
You mess with the peace...

14:27.640 --> 14:29.890
...and you mess with me!

14:35.270 --> 14:37.840
Bombs away!

14:37.840 --> 14:39.210
Eat this!

14:39.680 --> 14:40.280
Whoa!

14:42.650 --> 14:45.690
Oh, is it over? That was fast.

14:45.690 --> 14:47.830
Shut up, cake face.

14:47.830 --> 14:50.630
Your makeup looks like absolute shit.

14:50.630 --> 14:52.440
Screw you!

14:52.440 --> 14:55.040
It's way better than your lame-ass mask!

15:01.390 --> 15:04.390
Someone messed with the peace.

15:05.290 --> 15:06.300
Who was it?

15:08.750 --> 15:10.060
Huh?!

15:10.060 --> 15:12.130
What? Um, no!

15:12.130 --> 15:14.140
I haven't done anything
to mess with the peace!

15:14.140 --> 15:16.310
It wasn't even me who did that!

15:34.750 --> 15:38.930
THAT'S ENOUGH, YOU DIPSHITS!

15:45.240 --> 15:47.470
My head is killing me...

15:50.440 --> 15:53.470
Holy crap, seriously?
You guys drank way too much.

15:54.080 --> 15:57.150
This is your mess, too.
Don't pretend you weren't a part of it.

15:57.150 --> 15:59.400
That's cold! What the hell?!

15:59.400 --> 16:00.810
- Rick, you jackass!
- We're leaving.

16:00.810 --> 16:02.600
- Unbelievable...
- Get ready to go.

16:02.600 --> 16:04.600
Leave? And go where?

16:04.600 --> 16:05.670
To the Gate.

16:05.670 --> 16:07.130
The Gate?

16:07.130 --> 16:08.600
I see.

16:08.600 --> 16:10.990
So we're finally going back home
to our world?

16:10.990 --> 16:12.320
Nope.

16:12.320 --> 16:15.500
After everything that's happened,
they're gonna order us to go back.

16:16.000 --> 16:18.200
But not without Nanaue.

16:18.200 --> 16:20.750
And I don't know how long
it'll take us to rescue him,

16:21.270 --> 16:24.500
so we're going there to reset
the timer on your bombs.

16:25.080 --> 16:27.240
I'm quite sick of this bomb.

16:27.240 --> 16:29.260
It's the biggest pain
in the ass imaginable.

16:29.260 --> 16:31.640
Deadshot.
Go wake Peacemaker up.

16:31.640 --> 16:32.510
Uh... Okay.

16:32.510 --> 16:34.010
Just do it quietly.

16:34.010 --> 16:34.960
Huh?

16:40.680 --> 16:44.000
Are you sure about this?
Leaving the little guy behind?

16:44.000 --> 16:45.770
You seemed to love him so much.

16:45.770 --> 16:49.780
Yeah, but they'd probably dissect him
or something if I took him back with me.

16:50.240 --> 16:55.310
He can already fly freely over here.
And it looks like he made a friend too.

16:56.540 --> 16:59.790
Fair enough. We're going to get
locked up after we return, anyway.

16:59.790 --> 17:03.470
And it would be too cruel to make
our winged friend tag along.

17:03.470 --> 17:05.710
But my goodness, what a ride.

17:05.710 --> 17:08.520
We truly got the Isekai experience!

17:08.520 --> 17:13.640
Rescuing an old war buddy at the very end
would make a fantastic climax, but...

17:14.800 --> 17:18.330
In movie terms, it might be more exciting
for someone to take his place instead.

17:18.330 --> 17:20.440
Don't you jinx it.

17:20.440 --> 17:22.480
Anyways...

17:22.480 --> 17:24.690
I'm kinda confused.

17:24.690 --> 17:27.230
Why are we rescuing Nanaue?

17:27.230 --> 17:29.450
I figured you were gonna abandon him.

17:31.600 --> 17:35.250
Leaving Nanaue behind would
just cause problems for this world.

17:35.250 --> 17:37.720
Even though he's going
to get executed, regardless?

17:37.720 --> 17:40.460
I mean, that's what these bombs
are originally for, right?

17:45.850 --> 17:49.610
The bombs should
have been reset now... I think.

17:49.610 --> 17:50.590
Feel anything?

17:50.590 --> 17:51.810
Well...

17:56.720 --> 17:57.770
Seems okay.

17:57.770 --> 17:58.680
Good.

17:58.680 --> 17:59.960
Colonel Flag.

18:01.480 --> 18:02.270
I copy.

18:02.270 --> 18:02.960
What?!

18:02.960 --> 18:04.240
- A radio?!
- The timers have been reset.

18:04.240 --> 18:05.710
- You had one this whole time?!
- Are you near the Gate?

18:05.710 --> 18:07.610
- Sneaky bastard!
- Actually, ma'am...

18:10.320 --> 18:11.670
And that's my report.

18:11.670 --> 18:16.160
Frankly, I think it's impossible for us
to get any help from this world now.

18:16.650 --> 18:17.870
Understood.

18:17.870 --> 18:19.870
You have permission to return for now.

18:19.870 --> 18:22.610
You are to pass through
the Gate immediately.

18:22.610 --> 18:24.150
But ma'am, Nanaue...

18:24.150 --> 18:26.110
I mean, King Shark
is still in the Kingdom—

18:26.110 --> 18:28.160
I'll handle that problem from my end.

18:28.160 --> 18:29.590
Wait, does that mean?

18:30.090 --> 18:31.110
What?

18:31.110 --> 18:32.590
Are you kidding me? No way!

18:33.030 --> 18:33.720
This isn't good!

18:33.720 --> 18:34.270
Director...!

18:34.270 --> 18:36.690
I think we're in trouble! Hey, Rick!

18:36.690 --> 18:37.430
Ma'am!

18:56.200 --> 18:59.610
Director... Why'd you do that?

18:59.610 --> 19:03.120
I've determined this mission
has become too difficult to carry out.

19:03.120 --> 19:06.670
I'm going to close the Gate
once you come back.

19:06.670 --> 19:08.840
Make sure you leave no traces behind.

19:09.310 --> 19:10.630
So that's it?!

19:10.630 --> 19:12.190
You're just going to kill them all?!

19:12.190 --> 19:15.880
Are you going to squeeze as much information
out of me as you can and then kill me too?

19:15.880 --> 19:17.720
There's no need for me to get rid of you.

19:17.720 --> 19:19.640
- But even they have a right—
- Do it!

19:20.190 --> 19:22.350
Go ahead and do it,
you old fat bitch!

19:22.350 --> 19:25.840
Acting like you're hot shit
in that little cave of yours,

19:25.840 --> 19:29.560
thinking that you can
control the entire world!

19:29.560 --> 19:32.780
Enjoy that warped view of reality
until it comes back to bite you in the ass!

19:32.780 --> 19:35.070
Just stop talking!

19:35.070 --> 19:37.320
Get your hands off me, hypocrite!

19:37.320 --> 19:37.830
Hey!

19:37.830 --> 19:39.310
Look at that.

19:39.310 --> 19:40.470
I'll be damned.

19:40.470 --> 19:42.040
Please wait, Director!

19:42.490 --> 19:44.190
Ain't that the castle? It's burning.

19:44.190 --> 19:45.760
Smells like war.

19:45.760 --> 19:48.290
Director, let us continue the mission!

19:48.290 --> 19:50.370
There's a battle happening
in the royal capital.

19:50.370 --> 19:51.380
This is our chance!

19:52.880 --> 19:54.710
If we can drive the Empire back,

19:54.710 --> 19:57.280
and re-establish a friendly relationship
with the Kingdom

19:57.280 --> 19:58.950
then we can build a base in this world!

19:58.950 --> 20:00.970
You want this world's resources, right?!

20:02.970 --> 20:05.730
If we succeed,
we can complete the mission!

20:05.730 --> 20:08.890
And if we fail, we're all dead!
It works out either way!

20:08.890 --> 20:10.390
You have 24 hours.

20:11.290 --> 20:15.760
I just set the timer on the bombs
to explode in 24 hours.

20:15.760 --> 20:18.080
Show me the results before then.

20:18.640 --> 20:21.830
Fail to make it in time and they all die.
Which means...

20:22.290 --> 20:25.890
...you'll have no place to return to,
Colonel Flag.

20:30.560 --> 20:31.730
What's your deal?

20:31.730 --> 20:32.460
Huh?

20:32.910 --> 20:34.430
Why'd you save us?

20:35.990 --> 20:37.840
You're bad guys.

20:37.840 --> 20:40.470
Both in our world and in this one.

20:40.470 --> 20:41.470
Well, screw you, too.

20:41.470 --> 20:45.220
But over here,
you're a little on the good side.

20:45.720 --> 20:48.600
At least good enough
to have a song written about you.

20:50.850 --> 20:54.690
You talk like you're not
a bad guy yourself.

20:54.690 --> 20:57.120
Remember that brutal plan
we used against the elves?

20:57.120 --> 21:00.040
I seem to recall you admitting
you were a villain.

21:00.040 --> 21:01.090
No?

21:03.270 --> 21:05.030
What? What's the matter?

21:05.030 --> 21:07.020
Dude... Aren't you supposed to be dead?!

21:07.020 --> 21:09.120
I've been standing here
the whole time.

21:09.120 --> 21:11.030
But... Y-Your head—

21:11.030 --> 21:12.710
Oh, that?

21:12.710 --> 21:15.650
Just blowing off a body part or two
isn't enough to kill me.

21:15.650 --> 21:19.170
My heart, my brain...
I can position them wherever I desire.

21:20.850 --> 21:23.170
If the bomb was never a threat to you,

21:23.170 --> 21:25.040
then why did you go along
with the mission?

21:25.040 --> 21:26.200
Are you kidding?

21:26.200 --> 21:29.940
You can't very well have a story
without a protagonist, now can you?

21:29.940 --> 21:32.150
Are you guys ready to get serious?

21:32.610 --> 21:35.160
Because you've been pretty lame
supervillains so far.

21:35.160 --> 21:37.560
Personally, I'm sick of them.

21:38.130 --> 21:39.880
Both that damn Queen,

21:39.880 --> 21:42.910
and the bossy old hag
giving us ridiculous orders.

21:43.400 --> 21:45.870
That's why I'm gonna stick it to them.

21:45.870 --> 21:47.290
So, hey.

21:47.690 --> 21:50.330
Sorry to interrupt your
big badass speech, but...

21:50.330 --> 21:51.910
Are we gonna make it?

21:51.910 --> 21:53.670
We only have 24 hours.

21:53.670 --> 21:56.800
The royal capital is that teeny-tiny dot
in the distance, right?

22:01.080 --> 22:02.200
Let's hurry!

22:03.180 --> 22:05.680
2 HOURS AGO

22:05.680 --> 22:08.100
I have to do something.

22:08.100 --> 22:10.950
At the very least,
I have to stop the execution!

22:12.790 --> 22:14.810
Is my mother inside?

22:14.810 --> 22:15.790
Yes.

22:21.570 --> 22:22.490
Huh?

22:23.280 --> 22:26.090
What... happened here?

22:31.790 --> 22:33.460
Mother?

22:34.290 --> 22:36.670
Accursed humans.

22:36.670 --> 22:39.680
You'll pay for sabotaging my plans.
